    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia**_\n\nDocuments what went wrong when `stow -R emacs-modular` was run before `cutover`.\n\n- README: how to get pulled changes into Emacs (`git pull` in `~/dotfiles`, `stow -R` only when files are added or removed).\n- README: the \"cannot stow ... neither a link nor a directory\" error, its cause, and why not to use plain `stow`, `--adopt` or `yadm pull`.\n- `migrate.sh`: `STALE=ok` lets `dryrun`/`cutover` continue when home files are only older copies of repo files; the old versions still go to the backup.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edit (nightly routine owns it).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
